{"id":"3","category":"transit","planet":"Jupiter","zodiac_sign":"Taurus","house":null,"aspect":null,"traditional_effect":"Expansion and abundance","underlying_theme":"Present moment abundance","positive_interpretation":"Jupiter in Taurus suggests expansion is found in savoring the present moment fully. Abundance is not merely future gain but the richness available right now in sensory experience. This energy supports grounding your hopes into physical reality through mindful appreciation. By slowing down, you recognize that enoughness is already here. Growth happens when you nurture what exists rather than constantly chasing what is missing elsewhere.","growth_opportunity":"Finding richness in the now","practical_action":"Eat one meal slowly, focusing entirely on taste and texture","reflection_question":"Where do I feel lack when enoughness is already present?","encouraging_message":"Abundance is found in appreciating what is already here with you.","disclaimer":"This is a symbolic astrological interpretation, not a guaranteed outcome."}
